# Copy to `.env` and set values for your machine. `.env` is git-ignored;
# `.env.example` is the committed template and must contain no real values.
#
# Only EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables reach the app, and they are inlined into the JS
# bundle: anyone who inspects the app can read them. They are configuration,
# not secrets. Keep private keys, service accounts and server credentials on
# the server side. Git-ignoring `.env` does not make a client value secret.
#
# Read them only through src/config/env.ts (see docs/ENVIRONMENT.md). Add a new
# variable there, here, and in `.env`; restart `npx expo start` after changes.

# Which configuration set the app talks to: development | staging | production
EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development
